From: CHEN Xuan <chenxuan@iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] Use the legacy LLVM 23 HIP driver for RISC-V RDC links

LLVM 23's clang-linker-wrapper creates its host registration object with
empty CPU features, selecting the soft-float ABI on RISC-V. Linking this
object with the LP64D host libraries fails with both BFD and LLD.
The legacy HIP driver emits a correctly typed host registration object.
Select it for compile and link on RISC-V with Clang 23 only, preserving
all distribution flags and relocatable device code support.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -51,6 +51,15 @@
 
 project( rocfft LANGUAGES CXX C )
 
+# LLVM 23's new HIP linker wrapper emits a soft-float registration object on
+# RISC-V. The legacy HIP driver keeps the host LP64D ABI while retaining RDC.
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR STREQUAL "riscv64"
+   AND CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL "Clang"
+   AND CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_VERSION VERSION_GREATER_EQUAL "23"
+   AND CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_VERSION VERSION_LESS "24")
+  string(APPEND CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS " --no-offload-new-driver")
+endif()
+
 include(GNUInstallDirs)
 
 # This finds the rocm-cmake project, and installs it if not found
